  "idea": "Automated bug triage system that routes user reports directly to Linear",
  "text": "The automated bug report workflow that cuts engineering triage time by eighty percent. Developers lose whole afternoons context-switching between Slack pings, support tickets, and sprint backlogs. Unstructured bug reports lack critical user IDs and environment variables needed to reproduce issues. Build an automated triage flow that parses Intercom attachments, enriches user metadata, and assigns Linear priorities. You fix high-severity defects before churn happens.",
